{
  "_comment": "Post-land GPU smoke plan (runner: scripts/post_land_smoke.py; orchestrator: scripts/post-land-smoke.sh). Model paths come from the SMOKE_* environment variables named in each load (set per host in the orchestrator model-env files); model_bytes pins the artifact size. Artifact exceptions, all approved: the PP2 loads use the mq2-xts export because the mq4 split base (70.9 GB) cannot fit resident-expert PP2 on two 32 GB cards; the A3B load uses the canonical mq4r because the registry default mq4p is not present on the lane host; PLE is pinned to q4 on every Flash-Next load (the gfx1201 default is q8), so these cells are smoke pins, not claims about the full shipped defaults. KV mode, recurrent-state quantization and MTP depth are omitted so the shipped defaults apply. stderr_fail_patterns is empty on purpose: kernel faults are caught by the hold watcher, and route proofs are positive stderr_require/loaded_expect checks per load (there is no global 'no closed route plan' rejection: PP2, EP2 and A3B legitimately print it). xtx-d2 is disabled and path-filtered (see docs/post-land-smoke.md). Load names carry a -load suffix because the runner rejects a load and a cell sharing a name; pins and invariants use the cell names (fn1-ar, ep2-mtp, ...).",
